  </div>
  <div class="storylines-grid">
    <div class="story-card">
      <div class="story-num">Story 1</div>
      <h3>🇨🇻 Cape Verde: The Tiny Island That Captured the World</h3>
      <p>An island nation of 525,000 people, ranked 67th in the world, arrived at their first-ever World Cup and simply refused to leave. Cape Verde held Spain to a goalless draw, then pushed defending champions Argentina to extra time before falling 3–2. Their 40-year-old goalkeeper Vozinha became a cult hero. BBC Sport called them "the underdogs the World Cup will never forget."</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story-card">
      <div class="story-num">Story 2</div>
      <h3>🇩🇪 Germany Crashes Out — VAR Takes the Blame</h3>
      <p>Four-time champions Germany were eliminated in the Round of 32 by Paraguay on penalties after a controversial VAR call disallowed Jonathan Tah's extra-time header. Alan Shearer called it "a terrible decision." Paraguay, who had never won a World Cup knockout match before, stunned the Germans 4–3 on penalties — the biggest upset of the tournament.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story-card">
      <div class="story-num">Story 3</div>
      <h3>🇲🇦 Morocco Proves 2022 Wasn't a Fluke</h3>
      <p>After reaching the semifinals in Qatar, Morocco eliminated the Netherlands on penalties in the Round of 32, then thumped Canada 3–0 to reach the quarterfinals. They now face France in a rematch of the 2022 semifinal. Morocco has officially transitioned from Cinderella story to legitimate contender.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story-card">
      <div class="story-num">Story 4</div>
      <h3>🇦🇷 Messi's Historic Final Dance — and the Mbappé Rivalry</h3>
      <p>At 39, Messi became the first player to score 20 career World Cup goals and notched his first World Cup hat-trick against Algeria. Mbappé matched him at 7 goals this tournament. The Golden Boot race between the two — plus Haaland — is the tightest in World Cup history.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story-card">
      <div class="story-num">Story 5</div>
      <h3>📺 VAR Chaos: A Lottery, Not Justice</h3>
      <p>The tournament has been plagued by inconsistent VAR: Germany's disallowed winner, Vinícius Jr's goal ruled out, Ghana denied a clear penalty, Iran's winner disallowed by a millimeter. "Has VAR become a lottery?" asked BBC Sport. Pierluigi Collina has his work cut out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story-card">
      <div class="story-num">Story 6</div>
      <h3>🌎 Three Hosts, Three Knockout Berths</h3>
      <p>For the first time in World Cup history, every co-host advanced from the group stage. Mexico won their first knockout match since 1986. Canada won their first-ever knockout match. The USMNT faces Belgium tonight in a rematch of the 2014 classic. North America has delivered.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

